# Worker secrets. Cloudflare stores them write-only and cannot show them to you again, so keep a
# copy of whatever you generate. Copy this file to .dev.vars for `npm run dev`; for a deployed
# Worker set each one with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>`.

# Signs session cookies. Any long random string: `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Losing it signs every user out of every device.
SESSION_SECRET=""

# Web Push, for rest-timer alerts and workout-day reminders. Generate the pair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`. Losing them kills every existing subscription.
# Leave both empty to run without push notifications.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=""
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# Comma-separated user ids that get the admin dashboard. Leave empty on a fresh instance — you
# cannot know your own id until you have registered a profile. See worker/README.md.
# A uid is not a credential (it is useless without the matching passkey), but it is kept out of
# the repo so a reader cannot tell which account is worth attacking.
ADMIN_UIDS=""

# .dev.vars also overrides anything in `vars` for `wrangler dev`, which is how local development
# picks up settings the generic wrangler.jsonc deliberately leaves at their defaults. The smoke
# test in worker/test/ needs invite-only on to exercise the invite paths:
INVITE_ONLY=1
